},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Delaying work using a custom clock is beneficial when you need precise control over timing behavior,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as testing with test clocks or synchronizing work with specific time sources.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use this operator to implement retry backoff, throttling, or scheduled tasks that depend on a particular clock implementation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","text":"Example","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let start = Date()","let clock = SuspendingClock()","let delayedTask = DeferredTask {","    \"Delayed with custom clock\"","}.delay(for: .seconds(1), clock: clock, tolerance: .milliseconds(100))","let result = try await delayedTask.execute()","let elapsed = Date().timeIntervalSince(start)","print(\"Result: \\(result) after \\(elapsed) seconds\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Availability: macOS 13.0, iOS 16.0, watchOS 9.0, tvOS 16.0, visionOS 1.0 and above."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delay always waits out its whole duration, even when cancelled. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths"